  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Let d(C)d(C)d(C) denote the number of **distinct** elements in array CCC.\n\nFor a given array BBB of length MMM, score(B)=max⁡(d(C))\\text{score}(B) = \\max(d(C))score(B)=max(d(C)) across all CCC satisfying:\n\n\nCCC consists of MMM positive integers;\n1≤Ci≤Bi1\\le C_i \\le B_i1≤Ci​≤Bi​ for all 1≤i≤M1\\le i \\le M1≤i≤M;\nCCC is a **non-decreasing** array.\nYou are given an array AAA of size NNN and QQQ queries. For the ithi^{th}ith query:\n\n\nGiven two integers PiP_iPi​ and XiX_iXi​, update APiA_{P_i}APi​​ to XiX_iXi​;\nFind ∑i=1N∑j=iNscore(A[i,j])\\displaystyle{\\sum_{i=1}^{N} \\sum_{j=i}^{N} \\text{score}(A[i,j])}i=1∑N​j=i∑N​score(A[i,j]).\nNote that the updates to array AAA are **persistent**. This means that each update to AAA carries over to subsequent queries.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first line of each test case contains two positive integers NNN and QQQ −-− the size of array AAA and the number of queries.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers, A1,A2…ANA_1, A_2 \\ldots A_NA1​,A2​…AN​ −-− denoting the array AAA.\nEach of the next QQQ lines contains two space-separated integers PiP_iPi​ and XiX_iXi​ ––– the description of the ithi^{th}ith query.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each query, output on a new line, the required sum after updating APiA_{P_i}APi​​.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N,Q≤2⋅1051 \\leq N, Q \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N,Q≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai,Pi,Xi≤N1 \\leq A_i, P_i, X_i \\leq N1≤Ai​,Pi​,Xi​≤N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105.",
      "The sum of QQQ over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
