        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Given N=2N = 2N=2, Q=2Q = 2Q=2, and initial array A=[2,1]A = [2, 1]A=[2,1]. The queries are:\n\nP1=2P_1 = 2P1​=2, X1=2X_1 = 2X1​=2: Update A2A_2A2​ to 222, resulting in A=[2,2]A = [2, 2]A=[2,2]. We need to calculate sum of scores of all subarrays of AAA.\n\nscore([2])=1\\text{score}([2]) = 1score([2])=1. There are two occurrences if subarray [2][2][2].\nscore([2,2])=2\\text{score}([2,2]) = 2score([2,2])=2 since from array [2,2][2,2][2,2], we can create the array [1,2][1,2][1,2] with 222 distinct elements, satisfying all conditions.\nThus, the answer to the query is 1+1+2=41+1+2=41+1+2=4.\n\n\nP2=1P_2 = 1P2​=1, X2=1X_2 = 1X2​=1: Update A1A_1A1​ to 1, resulting in A=[1,2]A = [1, 2]A=[1,2]. We need to calculate sum of scores of all subarrays of AAA.\n\nscore([1])=score([2])=1\\text{score}([1]) = \\text{score}([2]) = 1score([1])=score([2])=1\nscore([1,2])=2\\text{score}([1,2]) = 2score([1,2])=2 since from array [1,2][1,2][1,2], we can create the array [1,2][1,2][1,2] with 222 distinct elements, satisfying all conditions.\nThus, the answer to the query is 1+1+2=41+1+2=41+1+2=4."
